{"id": "86091", "name": "דוגמה לפונקציה המקיימת f(a+b) = f(a) + f(b) (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Find a function of \\(f(x)\\) which satisfies</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(a+b)=f(a)+f(b) \\]</p><p>for all values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\).</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(f(x)=\\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Setting \\(a=b=0\\) shows that \\(f(0)=0\\); then we check that every line through the origin, \\(f(x)=kx\\), satisfies the condition.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — A necessary condition</b><br>Put \\(a=b=0\\) in the equation:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(0)=f(0)+f(0)\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad f(0)=0. \\]</p>So the graph of \\(f\\) must pass through the origin. In particular a line with a nonzero constant term, \\(f(x)=kx+c\\) with \\(c\\neq 0\\), does not work: then \\(f(a)+f(b)=k(a+b)+2c\\neq k(a+b)+c=f(a+b)\\).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — A line through the origin</b><br>Try \\(f(x)=kx\\) for a constant \\(k\\). For all \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), by the distributive law,<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(a+b)=k(a+b)=ka+kb=f(a)+f(b). \\]</p>So every function \\(f(x)=kx\\) satisfies the condition, and the answer is not unique: \\(f(x)=2x\\), \\(f(x)=-5x\\) and even \\(f(x)=0\\) are all correct. The simplest choice is \\(k=1\\):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(x)=x \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "p1:subst(a,x,ans1);\np2:subst(b,x,ans1);\np3:subst(a+b,x,ans1);", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "p1+p2", "tans": "p3", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": [], "nvariants": 1}